    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96324": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Hourly Student Employment - Front Desk Assistants Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Hourly Student Employment - Front Desk Assistants Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department STUDENT ENGAGEMENT Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Hourly Student Employment - Front Desk Assistants Posting Number 08525 Position Number 08525 Student Job Category Student - Hourly Job Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 2 Rate of Pay $10.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description ECU Department of Student Engagement is currently seeking several Front Desk Assistants. Students working in this position will serve as the first face students will see when entering the suite. Students working in this position will be approachable and willing to help student organizations leaders in the best way they can. Front Desk Assistant will assist with office functions such as: answering phones, picking up mail and packages, making copies for student organizations, giving student organization leaders access to lockers. These students will also be able to answer basic questions as it relates to Fraternity and Sorority Life councils and student organizations. Furthermore, students working in this position will become specialist of the Pirate Experience platform. They will be able to instruct tutorials/101s for student organizations on the basic functions of the Pirate Experience to aid in the successful management of their student organization, etc. Front Desk Assistant will also monitor the student engagement email account, checking the email throughout each shift, answering emails when possible, and/or forwarding emails to the proper channels when necessary such as specific questions about Greek organizations to the Fraternity and Sorority Life email and questions about general student organizations to the Student Organization Center email. Front Desk Assistant will aid in helping to maintain the cleanliness of the Student Engagement suite which will include helping to clean tables, straighten chairs, and ultimately making sure at the beginning and ending of each shift, the office reflects cleanliness. Other Front Desk Assistant may also be asked to participate in marketing, posting on social media, monitoring social media, and assisting with office branding. Students will participate in preparation for upcoming campus activities, involvement fairs, and programs. Students will perform other tasks as assigned. GPA Requirement Minimum of 2.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload a copy of your resume. Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96255 Open Date 08/13/2026 Close Date 09/26/2026 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Optional Documents Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
