      "title": "East Carolina University Portal | Federal Work Study (Off-Campus) - NC Stop Human Trafficking - Community Outreach/Public Relations Assistant",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Federal Work Study (Off-Campus) - NC Stop Human Trafficking - Community Outreach/Public Relations Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Federal Work Study (Off-Campus) - NC Stop Human Trafficking - Community Outreach/Public Relations Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department OFF CAMPUS STUDENT EMPLOYER Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Federal Work Study (Off-Campus) - NC Stop Human Trafficking - Community Outreach/Public Relations Assistant Posting Number 08380 Position Number 08380 Student Job Category Student - Federal Work Study Community Service Position Location Off-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 1 Rate of Pay $12.00 - $14.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description NC Stop Human Trafficking is seeking a community outreach assistant candidate who is dynamic and enjoys interacting with professionals, business people, and community members. This position requires attendance of various meetings and networking events. A successful community outreach assistant candidate must have good writing skills and willingness to learn how to use various platforms associated with NC Stop Human Trafficking’s digital outreach. Tasks include, but are not limited to: Daily Social Media posts Attend networking events Monthly e-newsletter Update website as needed Staff table at speaking engagements, community events GPA Requirement Minimum of 2.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please submit a hiring authorization, resume, cover letter, and three references to: Pam Strickland, pam@encstophumantrafficking.org An interview will be scheduled with selected applicants. The applicants are encouraged to bring evidence of their proficiency in the above. Please upload your Resume and Federal Work Study Authorization Form online. To be ELIGIBLE for FEDERAL WORK STUDY POSITIONS , students MUST QUALIFY and RECEIVE an AWARD from the ECU Financial Aid Office (Old Cafeteria Complex, 252-328-6610). Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95515 Open Date 07/27/2026 Close Date 04/01/2027 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you been approved for federal work study? (Please note that you will need to add your federal work study authorization form online). Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Federal Work Study Hiring Authorization Optional Documents Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
