    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95647": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Federal Work Study - Fitness Attendants Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Federal Work Study - Fitness Attendants Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department CAMPUS RECREATION AND WELLNESS Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Federal Work Study - Fitness Attendants Posting Number 08361 Position Number 08361 Student Job Category Student - Federal Work Study On-Campus Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 30 Rate of Pay $10.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description ECU Department of Campus Recreation and Wellness is currently seeking several Fitness Attendants. Join our dynamic team at Campus Recreation and Wellness ( CRW ) as a Fitness Attendant! CRW is dedicated to enhancing the recreation and wellness lifestyles of the ECU community through structured, self-directed, and educationally oriented programs. We aim to foster responsible citizenship, provide leadership experiences, and promote lifelong skills for physical, social, emotional, and mental well-being. Supporting the Division of Student Affairs’ commitment to purposeful well-being. Responsibilities (include but not limited to): Provide a world-class member experience with exercise education, equipment orientations, answering member questions, and managing emergencies Maintain and clean fitness equipment according to standards and protocols Utilize necessary software applications for facility operations Apply risk management strategies to protect everyone and minimize liability Identify and report potential hazards to ensure a safe environment Enhance your skills through professional development and training Use effective communication techniques with members and guests Adapt to various personality styles and backgrounds when assisting members Incorporate feedback to improve professionalism and future experiences Apply exercise science knowledge to assist members during workouts Perform other duties as assigned GPA Requirement Minimum of 2.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) Excellent communication skills Knowledge of fitness equipment and safety standards Ability to work independently and as part of a team for a minimum of 6 hours per week Must be CPR /First Aid/ AED certified or able to obtain certification within 60 days of hire Flexible work availability, including early mornings, nights, weekends, and ECU sanctioned breaks Demonstrated ability to manage and lift a minimum of 60 pounds. License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload your Resume, Federal Work Study Hiring Authorization Form and a copy of your class schedule online. To be ELIGIBLE for FEDERAL WORK STUDY POSITIONS , students MUST QUALIFY and RECEIVE an AWARD from the ECU Financial Aid Office (Old Cafeteria Complex, 252-328-6610.) Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95478 Open Date 07/24/2026 Close Date 04/01/2027 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have any related certifications? If so, please list those certifications as well as the expiration date. (Open Ended Question) * What is your anticipated Graduation Date? (Open Ended Question) * Please list: what days and times that you are available to work during the current Semester. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Federal Work Study Hiring Authorization Optional Documents Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
