    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96589": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal | Director of IT Enterprise Data Services",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Director of IT Enterprise Data Services Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Director of IT Enterprise Data Services Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position requires the employee to reside within a reasonable commutable distance of the ECU main campus. “Reasonable commuting distance” is defined as a location that does not exceed a distance that can be safely traveled in two hours by automobile under average conditions of traffic, weather, and roads to employee’s assigned duty station in Greenville, NC. This position may be eligible for Flexible Work Arrangements (FWA) under the ECU FWA Policy. East Carolina University requires applicants to submit a candidate profile online in order to be considered for the position. Candidates must also submit a cover letter, resume, and a list of three references, including contact information, online. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Contingent upon availability of funds. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Director of IT Enterprise Data Services Position Number 500705 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Department AFH IT Enterprise Data Serv Department Homepage https://itcs.ecu.edu/ Advertising Department ITCS DATA SERVICES Division Administration & Finance Classification Title IT Manager III Working Title Director of IT Enterprise Data Services Number of Vacancies 1 Full Time Equivalent (FTE) 1.00 Full Time or Part Time Full Time Anticipated Recruitment Range. Salary offered may be outside of this range as impacted by budget, UNC salary administration, and/or candidate qualifications. $135,000 -$160,000 Position Location (City) Greenville Position Type Non-Faculty Job Category Non-Faculty Professional Be a Pirate! Be a Pirate! East Carolina University ( ECU ) is consistently ranked among the nation’s top public universities for its commitment to research, innovation, social mobility, and public service. Classified as a R1 institution by the Carnegie Commission on Higher Education, ECU is among the top 5% of research universities in the United States, an elite designation reflecting the highest levels of research activity, funding, and doctoral output. Founded in 1907, ECU is a public, four-year university located in Greenville, N.C. , which and is widely regarded as the cultural, educational, economic, and medical hub of eastern North Carolina. Through education, research, healthcare, community engagement, athletics, cultural enrichment, and service, ECU enhances the quality of life for its students, the state and communities around the world. It is a great place to work, teach, and learn. ECU’s commitment to impactful scholarship is further demonstrated through its repeated Carnegie Community Engagement Classification (2010, 2015, 2024), as well as its 2024 designation as a Carnegie Leadership for Public Purpose institution. These distinctions recognize the university’s leadership in translating research into meaningful community partnerships and measurable societal benefits. The university supports its workforce through a wide range of professional development opportunities designed to foster career growth and skill advancement. Eligible employees also benefit from a comprehensive benefits package that promotes a healthy work-life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Information Technology and Computing Services ( ITCS ) is the central agency that supports enterprise-wide computing at East Carolina University. ITCS , through innovative information technology initiatives and service, provides opportunities for the ECU community to excel in teaching, research, and service using state-of-the-market technology and collaborative environments. ITCS is first and foremost committed to providing excellent information technology support for faculty, staff, and students. ITCS partners with campus departments, other universities, and industry to make strategic investments in information technology infrastructure that will help maintain a competitive advantage in administrative applications, faculty research, and outreach to the state and nation. We will achieve this through increasing the core functions and deploying appropriate technology throughout the university. Enterprise Data Services provides enterprise data management, governance, analytics, reporting, and database administration services for ECU . The team develops and supports data platforms and business intelligence solutions that enable data-informed decision-making, improve operational effectiveness, and ensure the university’s data assets are secure, trusted, and strategically managed. Primary Purpose of Position The Director of Enterprise Data Services provides strategic leadership and oversight for the university’s enterprise data, reporting, analytics, and database environments. This position is responsible for establishing the vision, policies, standards, and long-term operational strategies that guide the management and use of institutional data as a strategic asset. The Director leads the ITCS Enterprise Data Services team and is accountable for the planning, delivery, security, governance, and continuous improvement of enterprise data platforms, including data warehousing, operational data stores, database systems, business intelligence and reporting environments, analytics platforms, and emerging data technologies. Working closely with executive leadership, academic and administrative units, and external partners, the Director translates institutional priorities and business requirements into technology-enabled data solutions that support decision-making, operational effectiveness, regulatory compliance, and strategic planning. The position is responsible for developing and executing short- and long-term plans related to staffing, budgeting, technology investments, service delivery, and organizational capability development. The Director also serves as the university’s primary liaison for enterprise data initiatives with regulatory agencies, peer institutions, professional organizations, and technology vendors. The position is responsible for developing and executing short- and long-term plans related to enterprise data strategy, governance, analytics, artificial intelligence readiness, staffing, budgeting, technology investments, service delivery, and organizational capability development. The Director also serves as the university’s primary liaison for enterprise data, analytics, and data governance initiatives with peer institutions, professional organizations, technology vendors, and strategic partners. Strategic Leadership and Data Innovation: Provides leadership for enterprise data strategy, governance, analytics, reporting, and database services by establishing organizational direction, identifying emerging trends, and aligning technology capabilities with institutional priorities. Develops and maintains strategic roadmaps for enterprise data platforms, business intelligence, analytics, and governance programs. Cultivates partnerships with campus stakeholders, higher education institutions, technology providers, and professional organizations to advance data-driven decision-making and innovation. Leads university-wide initiatives involving enterprise data, reporting, analytics, and database technologies. Provides executive oversight for the evaluation, design, implementation, and optimization of solutions that support the university’s academic, administrative, and research missions. Ensures enterprise data services effectively support institutional needs for data integration, reporting, analytics, governance, compliance, and operational decision support. Recommends organizational, administrative, and operational improvements to enhance the effectiveness, reliability, and scalability of data services. Data Governance, Policy, and Compliance: Leads the development and implementation of enterprise policies, standards, and best practices governing the management, security, quality, accessibility, and use of institutional data. Collaborates with university stakeholders to establish and maintain a comprehensive data governance framework that promotes data stewardship, accountability, consistency, and trust across the institution. Ensures compliance with applicable federal and state regulations, UNC System policies, audit recommendations, and industry best practices related to data management, privacy, security, retention, and reporting. Provides guidance and oversight for governance processes, data standards, metadata management, data quality initiatives, and enterprise reporting practices. Enterprise Project and Portfolio Leadership: Serves as executive sponsor for strategic and operational initiatives involving enterprise data, analytics, reporting, and database technologies. Collaborates with ITCS leadership, the Central Project Office, and campus stakeholders to ensure projects align with institutional goals, technology standards, and resource priorities. Provides executive oversight for project portfolios, including prioritization, resource allocation, risk management, and performance monitoring. Regularly communicates project status, challenges, opportunities, and outcomes to the Chief Information Officer and other university leaders. Ensures projects are adequately staffed, effectively governed, and delivered in accordance with established objectives, timelines, and service expectations. Organizational and Staff Leadership: Provides overall leadership, direction, and management for the Enterprise Data Services organization. Establishes operational priorities, performance expectations, service standards, and workforce development strategies that support reliable and customer-focused service delivery. Directs the recruitment, development, mentoring, and retention of professional staff while fostering a culture of collaboration, innovation, accountability, and continuous improvement. Oversees employee performance management, succession planning, training programs, and career development initiatives. Evaluates organizational effectiveness and implements improvements to ensure the unit remains responsive to evolving institutional and technology needs. Financial and Resource Management: Develops and manages the Enterprise Data Services budget and multi-year investment plans in support of institutional priorities and technology strategy. Evaluates funding requirements for infrastructure, software, professional services, staffing, capacity growth, modernization initiatives, and operational sustainability. Provides oversight for procurement activities, contract negotiations, vendor management, and technology licensing agreements. Ensures responsible stewardship of university resources while maximizing operational efficiency, service quality, and long-term value. Monitors expenditures, forecasts future needs, and aligns resource allocation with strategic objectives and service commitments. Key Outcomes: The Director ensures that ECU’s enterprise data ecosystem is secure, reliable, scalable, well-governed, and aligned with institutional goals. Through leadership in governance, analytics, database services, and strategic planning, the position enables data-informed decision-making, supports operational excellence, enhances institutional effectiveness, and advances the university’s mission through the responsible use of data and technology. The standard work schedule for this position will need to be adjusted to meet the position requirements, which include and are not limited to evening and weekend hours to perform scheduled and unscheduled workload requirements to maintain University operations. Minimum Education, Knowledge, Skills, and Experience Bachelor’s degree and 4 years of relevant experience or equivalent combination of education and experience. License or Certification Required by Statute or Regulation NA Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills, and Experience Preferred Education, Knowledge, Experience: Master’s degree and 2 years of relevant experience. A minimum of 1 year of supervisory or team leadership experience. Demonstrated leadership experience managing enterprise data services, analytics, business intelligence, data warehousing, database administration, artificial intelligence initiatives, or related functions in a large and complex organization. Extensive knowledge of enterprise data governance frameworks, data stewardship practices, data quality management, data classification, metadata management and master data management, and data security principles. Experience developing and implementing enterprise data strategies, analytics programs, business intelligence capabilities, using cloud based platforms such as Microsoft Fabric, Power BI, or similar technologies. Strong understanding of database technologies, data integration architectures, ETL / ELT processes, data engineering practices, enterprise data platform management, and modern analytics ecosystems. Ability to establish data standards, performance metrics, and governance processes that promote consistent, trusted, and accessible institutional data. Experience leading cross-functional teams and collaborating with executive leadership, academic units, administrative departments, and external partners to support strategic decision-making. Demonstrated experience serving as a strategic advisor to executive leadership on data-informed decision-making, performance measurement, analytics, governance, and technology investments. Excellent communication and relationship-building skills with the ability to present complex technical and analytical concepts to executive, operational, and non-technical audiences. Experience developing roadmaps, prioritizing competing initiatives, managing budgets, and aligning technology investments with organizational goals. Understanding of regulatory, privacy, security, and compliance requirements associated with institutional data management. Ability to foster a culture of innovation, continuous improvement, data literacy, and evidence-based decision-making across the organization. Experience building and mentoring high-performing technical and analytics teams while promoting collaboration, accountability, and customer-focused service delivery. Strong combination of leadership, technical, analytical, and strategic planning skills with demonstrated experience leading enterprise data and analytics functions within a complex organization. Expertise in data governance, business intelligence, data management, and enterprise reporting, along with the ability to translate institutional priorities into actionable data strategies and solutions. Ability to be a strategic leader who can balance technical excellence, governance, operational effectiveness, and stakeholder engagement while advancing the institution’s enterprise data strategy and enabling data-informed decision-making at all levels of the organization. Special Instructions to Applicant This position requires the employee to reside within a reasonable commutable distance of the ECU main campus. “Reasonable commuting distance” is defined as a location that does not exceed a distance that can be safely traveled in two hours by automobile under average conditions of traffic, weather, and roads to employee’s assigned duty station in Greenville, NC. This position may be eligible for Flexible Work Arrangements ( FWA ) under the ECU FWA Policy. East Carolina University requires applicants to submit a candidate profile online in order to be considered for the position. Candidates must also submit a cover letter, resume, and a list of three references, including contact information, online. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Contingent upon availability of funds. Additional Instructions to Applicant In order to be considered for this position, applicants must complete a candidate profile online via the PeopleAdmin system and submit any requested documents. Additionally, applicants that possess the preferred education and experience must also possess the minimum education/experience, if applicable. Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Job Open Date 08/20/2026 Open Until Filled No Job Close Date - Positions will be posted until 11:59 p.m. EST on this date. If no closing date is indicated, the position may close at any time after the initial screening date. 09/18/2026 Initial Screening Begins 09/03/2026 Rank Level Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96584 Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu. Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you now or in the future require visa sponsorship for employment? Yes No * Are you willing to relocate to the local area to maintain a physical presence in the Department? Yes No * Please indicate where you learned about this job vacancy. LinkedIn Chronicle of Higher Education CareerBuilder Greenville Daily Reflector Raleigh News & Observer HigherEdJobs.com InsideHigherEd.com Monster.com Indeed ECU Website Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
