    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95679": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Federal Work Study - Administrative Assistants Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Federal Work Study - Administrative Assistants Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please upload your resume and Federal Work Study Authorization Form online. To be considered for FEDERAL WORK STUDY positions, students MUST BE QUALIFIED AND RECEIVE A FEDERAL WORK STUDY AWARD from the ECU Financial Aid Office (Old Cafeteria Complex, 252-328-6610.) Position Details Position Information Advertising Department REGISTRAR Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Federal Work Study - Administrative Assistants Posting Number 08374 Position Number 08374 Student Job Category Student - Federal Work Study On-Campus Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 2 Rate of Pay $11.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description ECU Department of the Registrar is currently seeking several Administrative Assistants. On a daily basis, Administrative Assistants would be expected to: Scan physical records into Xtender Ensure integrity of scanned images (i.e., clear and legible; matching student information) Utilize Banner for student record verification Perform file maintenance and organization Admin Assistants may also be asked to perform other duties as assigned. The Office of the Registrar is located a short walk from main campus in the Uptown/Downtown district at 207 E Fifth Street. The office is open Monday through Friday, 8:00 am to 5:00 pm. Admin Assistants should expect to work up to 20 hours a week with the possibility of up to 24 hours a week if warranted. GPA Requirement Minimum of 2.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) Candidates should Possess an understanding of scanning equipment and software, or an ability to learn the skills necessary to successfully work with scanning technology Possess organizational skills Demonstrate attention to detail/be detail-oriented Demonstrate the ability to manage multiple tasks Demonstrate the ability to be courteous and professional in a collegial/professional environment Be willing to work with student records and uphold privacy regulations regarding Personal Identifying Information ( PII ) Additionally, all applicants should be enrolled as a student and be in good academic standing with East Carolina University, as well as local, state, and federal laws. Additionally, candidates must possess a minimum cumulative GPA of a 2.00. Rate of pay: $10-$12 per hour, based on experience. License/certification required None Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload your resume and Federal Work Study Authorization Form online. To be ELIGIBLE for FEDERAL WORK STUDY POSITIONS , students MUST QUALIFY and RECEIVE an AWARD from the ECU Financial Aid Office (Old Cafeteria Complex, 252-328-6610.) Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95511 Open Date 07/24/2026 Close Date 04/01/2027 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you been approved for federal work study? (Please note that you will need to add your federal work study authorization form online). Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Federal Work Study Hiring Authorization Optional Documents Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
