      "title": "East Carolina University Portal",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Hourly Student Employment - Undergraduate Learning Assistants Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Hourly Student Employment - Undergraduate Learning Assistants Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department PHYSICS, DEPT OF Academic Term/Year FALL 2026 Position Title Hourly Student Employment - Undergraduate Learning Assistants Posting Number 08433 Position Number 08433 Student Job Category Student - Hourly Job Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 6 Rate of Pay $12.50/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? Yes Job Description ECU Department of Physics is currently seeking several Undergraduate Learning Assistants (LA) for PHYS 2350 and PHYS 2360-Fall 2026. Student must have completed the course for which they will serve as an LA. The commitment is 5 hours per week (three classroom hours, one prep meeting with the instructor, and one hour of individual preparation). Duties: Attend classes within the assigned discipline to interact with students and lead discussions about class material. Attend a prep session with the faculty member teaching the class they are serving. New LAs must attend an orientation/training session to be held early in the semester. Expected Products: Learning Assistants are expected to bring all prepared materials with them to class so they may work with students. They do not need to generate any reports or other artifacts. Evaluation Metrics: Meet with designated instructor near the end of semester to discuss strengths/weaknesses of LA. Give LA constructive feedback. GPA Requirement Minimum of 3.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) Completed 30 scheduled hours of credit, and Enrolled in at least 6 scheduled hours for the Fall 2026 semester License/certification required N/A Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload your resume online. Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95779 Open Date 07/31/2026 Close Date 09/11/2026 Open Until Filled Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is/are your major(s) and minor(s)? (Open Ended Question) What days/times are you NOT available? (We will have access to your class schedule and will not schedule you for LA duties during any of your classes.) (Open Ended Question) What is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) Will you be employed elsewhere on campus during the Spring 2026 semester? (If yes, indicate where you will be employed.) (Open Ended Question) Have you previously been an LA? If yes, indicate which semesters and courses. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Transcripts List of References Additional Document #1 Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
