    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96647": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal | Federal Work Study - Lab Assistant",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Federal Work Study - Lab Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Federal Work Study - Lab Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department BIOLOGY, DEPT OF Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Federal Work Study - Lab Assistant Posting Number 08574 Position Number 08574 Student Job Category Student - Federal Work Study On-Campus Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 1 Rate of Pay $10.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description ECU Department of Biology is currently seeking a student to serve as an Undergraduate Genomics Core Lab Assistant for the preparation of materials used in teaching labs. Lab assistants are responsible for: • The preparation of reagents • Laboratory setup • Laboratory breakdown • Maintaining teaching labs for biochemistry and biotechnology • Cleaning teaching laboratories The student must also be available to work a minimum of 4 hours a week around their class schedule. GPA Requirement Minimum of 2.5 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) Preferred majors: Biology,Biochemistry,Chemistry No experience required this could be an excellent resume builder as you will learn lab principles and techniques and receive multiple trainings. License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload your Resume, Course Schedule and Federal Work Study Hiring Authorization Form online. To be ELIGIBLE for FEDERAL WORK STUDY POSITIONS , students MUST QUALIFY and RECEIVE an AWARD from the ECU Financial Aid Office (Old Cafeteria Complex, 252-328-6610.) Additional Instructions t