    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96093": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Federal Work Study (Off-Campus) - Building Hope Community Life Center - Academic Support Staff Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Federal Work Study (Off-Campus) - Building Hope Community Life Center - Academic Support Staff Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department OFF CAMPUS STUDENT EMPLOYER Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Federal Work Study (Off-Campus) - Building Hope Community Life Center - Academic Support Staff Posting Number 08491 Position Number 08491 Student Job Category Student - Federal Work Study Community Service Position Location Off-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 5 Rate of Pay $12.00 - $14.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description Building Hope Community Life Center is currently seeking Academic Support Staff to serve as an integral member of the Building Hope Community Life Center team by providing academic assistance, classroom support, and student engagement services for elementary and middle school students participating in Building Hope’s after-school and enrichment programs. This position supports the organization’s mission of empowering youth through academic excellence, character development, faith-based values, and meaningful community engagement. Work-study students will gain practical experience in education, nonprofit leadership, youth development, and community service while developing professional skills that prepare them for future careers. Academic Support Assist students with homework, reading, mathematics, science, and writing assignments. Provide one-on-one and small-group tutoring. Reinforce classroom instruction through educational games and hands-on activities. Encourage positive study habits and academic accountability. Support literacy initiatives, including reading across the curriculum. Classroom & Program Support Prepare classrooms and learning materials before the program begins. Assist with STEAM , literacy, SEL , and enrichment activities. Monitor students during transitions, snack, recreation, and dismissal. Help maintain a clean, organized, and engaging learning environment. Support lesson plan implementation under staff supervision. Student Engagement Build positive relationships with students. Encourage respectful behavior and positive conflict resolution. Serve as a positive role model reflecting Building Hope’s mission and values. Promote student participation and confidence. Administrative Support Assist with attendance and sign-in/out procedures. Prepare copies, learning packets, and educational resources. Organize supplies and classroom materials. Assist with data entry and program documentation. Support special events, family nights, and community programs. Special Events Assist staff during: Family Engagement Events Community Outreach Activities Back-to-School Bash Holiday Programs Summer Camp Field Trips Volunteer Projects Minimum Qualifications Applicants must: Be eligible for Federal Work-Study through their college or university. Be enrolled in good academic standing. Have excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Demonstrate professionalism and reliability. Enjoy working with children. Be able to maintain confidentiality. Pass all required background checks. GPA Requirement Minimum of 2.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Reginald Barrett – Program Director reginald@buildinghopenc.org 252 757 1840 Please send a resume to the above email address. Please upload your Resume and Federal Work Study Authorization Form online. To be ELIGIBLE for FEDERAL WORK STUDY POSITIONS , students MUST QUALIFY and RECEIVE an AWARD from the ECU Financial Aid Office (Old Cafeteria Complex, 252-328-6610). Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96057 Open Date 08/04/2026 Close Date 04/01/2027 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you been approved for federal work study? (Please note that you will need to add your federal work study authorization form online). Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Federal Work Study Hiring Authorization Optional Documents Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
