    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96670": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Hourly Student Employment - Greenhouse Assistants Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Hourly Student Employment - Greenhouse Assistants Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department BIOLOGY, DEPT OF Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Hourly Student Employment - Greenhouse Assistants Posting Number 08508 Position Number 08508 Student Job Category Student - Hourly Job Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 2 Rate of Pay $11.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description ECU Department of Biology is currently seeking several Greenhouse Assistants. Undergraduate greenhouse weekend waters will water the assigned Howell Sci Complex greenhouse plants on weekends, when the greenhouse manager is out sick/on vacation/off-campus, and on holidays including academic summer and winter break. They will alternate assigned watering days with other greenhouse assistants in a flexible reservation system with communication ahead of time provided. Monthly hours range between 1 hr to 4 hrs, depending on worker availability and greenhouse productivity. GPA Requirement Minimum of 2.5 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) Biology Earth & Atmospheric Sciences Environmental Studies - Ideal candidates must be reliable and communicate quickly when problems arise. The job does not require many hours in a typical month, but the short period of time when plants are watered is important. - Communication with the greenhouse manager should be expected during assigned weekends. - Lab-specific greenhouse training will be provided with position on greenhouse management and safety training. If you say you will water the plants between 8-11AM and 3-6PM on the weekend, you must water or tell the greenhouse manager ASAP when you realize you cannot, or the plants that grad students and researchers base their research on will become damaged. Poor communication or slacking in duties will result in immediate job loss. License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload your resume online. Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96135 Open Date 08/10/2026 Close Date 09/24/2026 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these 