    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95918": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Motorcoach Driver (Temporary) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Motorcoach Driver (Temporary) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Position Details Position Information Job Title Motorcoach Driver (Temporary) Position Number T17123 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Department AFH Transit and Safe Ride Department Homepage https://transit.ecu.edu/ Advertising Department TRANSIT Division Administration & Finance Classification Title Vehicle/Equipment Operator Competency Level 2 - Journey Working Title Motorcoach Driver (Temporary) Number of Vacancies 25 Full Time Equivalent (FTE) 1.0 Full time or Part time Full Time Hourly Salary Rate/Range $25.00 Position Location (City) Greenville Position Type Temporary Staff Job Category Staff - Temporary Be a Pirate! Be a Pirate! East Carolina University ( ECU ) is consistently ranked among the nation’s top public universities for its commitment to research, innovation, social mobility, and public service. Classified as a R1 institution by the Carnegie Commission on Higher Education, ECU is among the top 5% of research universities in the United States, an elite designation reflecting the highest levels of research activity, funding, and doctoral output. Founded in 1907, ECU is a public, four-year university located in Greenville, N.C. , which and is widely regarded as the cultural, educational, economic, and medical hub of eastern North Carolina. Through education, research, healthcare, community engagement, athletics, cultural enrichment, and service, ECU enhances the quality of life for its students, the state and communities around the world. It is a great place to work, teach, and learn. ECU’s commitment to impactful scholarship is further demonstrated through its repeated Carnegie Community Engagement Classification (2010, 2015, 2024), as well as its 2024 designation as a Carnegie Leadership for Public Purpose institution. These distinctions recognize the university’s leadership in translating research into meaningful community partnerships and measurable societal benefits. The university supports its workforce through a wide range of professional development opportunities designed to foster career growth and skill advancement. Eligible employees also benefit from a comprehensive benefits package that promotes a healthy work-life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit ECU Transit is the university’s transportation system. We serve students, faculty, and visitors through free fixed-route and on-demand services designed to make getting around campus easier. The system is run predominantly by more than 100 student employees. The mission of ECU Transit is to provide transportation services, which are safe, dependable and cost effective to the University community, and to facilitate learning and involvement for student success thereby enhancing the quality of life in our community. Primary Purpose of Position This position serves as a motorcoach operator, reporting to the Transit Charter Services Manager. This is a temporary position, and employment may not exceed 11 months in a calendar year. The position will be responsible for the safe operation of a 45-foot motorcoach bus with responsibility to the chartering group and the University in adherence to Federal Motor Carrier Safety Regulations and other state and local traffic laws. Working hours will vary based on trip assignments but may include multiple day trips away from Greenville as well as single day trips. The following is a detailed list of duties required for this role: Safe Operation: The position will be required to comply with all Federal Motor Carrier Safety Regulations for interstate transportation including but not limited to hours-of-service regulations, fit-for-duty regulations, medical certification, as well as vehicle safety inspections. Operators must exercise good judgement, safe vehicle operation and defensive driving skills, and positively represent the Department and the University. The position will adjust driving for various weather conditions and traffic situations. Passenger Management/Customer Service: Will provide excellence in customer service and sound decision-making under pressure. Greets passengers and groups in a courteous manner and assists with boarding and disembarking. Ensures passenger safety and comfort throughout the journey. Addresses any concerns or issues raised by passengers and provides necessary assistance. Operate a wheelchair lift, secure passengers’ mobility devices, and assist passengers with disabilities with boarding, riding, and alighting in a safe manner when necessary. Expected to help passengers with baggage loading and unloading Route Planning & Management: Plan a safe driving route for trips & manage changing conditions on roadways. Demonstrates complete knowledge about the geographic area surrounding Greenville. and trip destinations Communicate any delays or changes to passengers in a clear and timely manner. Vehicle Maintenance: Perform routine pre-trip and post-trip inspections of motorcoach vehicles. Ensures vehicle is adequately stocked with supplies for trip duration. Report any mechanical issues or concerns to maintenance team for repairs. Keep the interior and exterior of the vehicle clean and presentable while on assignment. Administrative Duties: Write reports and complete forms as required: May prepare detailed written reports concerning accidents/incidents, breakdowns, and mechanical defects as required at the end of a shift. Complete driving logs while on trips, adhering to hours-of-service requirements Maintains an accurate record of mileage, fuel consumption and any incidents during trips. Training of Motorcoach Operators: May be tasked to assist with the training of newly hired motorcoach operators including but not limited to classroom instruction, hands on/behind the wheel exercises and practical experience in various driving scenarios according to all local/state and federal regulations. Other Duties as Assigned: Will perform physical tasks related to vehicle inspections, baggage handling, and operation of the motorcoach vehicle. Complete ongoing training courses for professional development provided by ECU Transit during the duration of employment. Team meetings Monthly Safety Meetings Fixed Route Driving Assignments Other duties as assigned. Minimum Education, Knowledge, Skills, and Experience Demonstrated possession of the competencies necessary to perform the work. Requires appropriate licenses or certifications to operate assigned types of vehicles or equipment. License or Certification Required by Statute or Regulation Class B, or A, CDL with Passenger Endorsement & No Air Brake Restriction License or Certification Required by the Department A valid NC Commercial Driver’s License, Class B or A, with passenger endorsement and without air brake restriction and the ability to drive Interstate (no K-restriction). A Valid DOT Commercial Driver Medical Certificate ( MEC ) Form MCSA -5876. Entry Level Driver Training Certification, if CDL was obtained after February 2022. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills, and Experience Previous experience operating a motorcoach vehicle, including interstate trips. Special Instructions to Applicant Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Additional Instructions to Applicant In order to be considered for this position, applicants must complete a candidate profile online via the PeopleAdmin system and submit any requested documents. Additionally, applicants that possess the preferred education and experience must also possess the minimum education/experience, if applicable. Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Job Open Date 01/16/2026 Open Until Filled No Job Close Date 12/21/2026 Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/91008 Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu. Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate where you learned about this job vacancy. LinkedIn Chronicle of Higher Education CareerBuilder Greenville Daily Reflector Raleigh News & Observer HigherEdJobs.com InsideHigherEd.com Monster.com Indeed ECU Website Other * Driver's License Number? (Open Ended Question) * License classification? (Open Ended Question) * License endorsements? (Open Ended Question) * Which state issued your drivers license? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Cover Letter List of References Licenses/Certifications Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96434": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Student Employment - Study Hall Monitors Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Student Employment - Study Hall Monitors Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department STUDENT DEVELOPMENT Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Student Employment - Study Hall Monitors Posting Number 08324 Position Number 08324 Student Job Category Student - Hourly Job Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 10 Rate of Pay $9.00 - $10.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description ECU Department of Student Development – Athlete Academic Services is currently seeking several Study Hall Monitors. Expectations: Study Hall Monitors conduct study hall according to the guidelines established by the Office of Student-Athlete Academic Services. Students in this position help to maintain a productive study environment by tracking attendance, managing room reservations, and enforcing policies. GPA Requirement Minimum of 3.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) For hiring consideration, applicants must: Be enrolled ECU students. Have a minimum of 1 full time 4-year college semester completed or hold degree (e.g. associate’s, bachelor’s, etc.) 3.0 GPA is preferred License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload your Resume online Academic references should be provided and a reference check will be conducted as a part of the screening process. Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/94794 Open Date 06/29/2026 Close Date 10/02/2026 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please select any of the groups with which you are affiliated Current ECU Student-Athlete Former ECU Student-Athlete Athletic training staff/student staff ECU athletics team manager Member of ECU varsity cheer Member of ECU varsity Dance member of ECU Marching Pirates/Pep Band ECU Athletic Department Intern/GA ECU athletics rostered practice player None of these apply to me. * What is your anticipated Graduation Date? (Open Ended Question) * Indicate your current degree program. If a graduate student, please list your undergraduate and graduate degrees(ex. BS-Finance, pursing MBA) (Open Ended Question) * Have you been employed with ECU in the last 3 years? yes no * Do you intend to or have you applied for one of our other student positions (study hall monitor, assistant learning specialist, or tutor/mentor) Yes No * Do you have other current campus employment or have you been offered a position for the current/upcoming semester? Yes No * This position works toward having consistent weekly hours. From the following shifts, which do you feel you would be able to work consistently each week. \r\nSundays 6-9pm\r\nMondays through Thursdays 8am-12:30pm, 12:30-5pm, 5-9pm\r\nFridays 8-11am, 11am-2pm (Open Ended Question) * Provide an academic reference. Include their name, email, phone number and how you know the individual.\r\n(Example: Dr. John Doe, jdoe@school.edu, 555-555-5555, COAD instructor) (Open Ended Question) * Provide an academic reference. Include their name, email, phone number and how you know the individual. (Example: Dr. John Doe, jdoe@school.edu, 555-555-5555, COAD instructor) (Open Ended Question) * I agree to allow the Office of Student-Athlete Academic Services, Department of Athletics at East Carolina University, to conduct a review of my grades and references to determine my eligibility for employment. I agree I disagree * I understand that my student record pertaining to violations related to the ECU Student Code of Conduct and Academic Integrity, housed in the Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities, will be checked to determine if I meet the minimum expectations for employment by the Office of Student-Athlete Academic Services. I understand. * I certify that the information I have provided in this application is true and correct to the best of my knowledge and ability and I have not knowingly falsified any personal information. yes no Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Letter of Recommendation Optional Documents Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
