    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95670": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal | Federal Work Study - Career Peers Front Desk Assistant",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Federal Work Study - Career Peers Front Desk Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Federal Work Study - Career Peers Front Desk Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department CAREER SERVICES Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Federal Work Study - Career Peers Front Desk Assistant Posting Number 08399 Position Number 08399 Student Job Category Student - Federal Work Study On-Campus Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 1 Rate of Pay $12.00/Hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description ECU Department of Career Services is currently seeking a Career Peers Front Desk Assistant. SCOPE OF POSITION Students hired for this position will work in two functions; student experience expert and outreach specialist. As a student experience expert, Career Peers will be trained to develop and maintain in-depth awareness of the wide-range of programs and services offered through Career Service’s main office, its multiple satellite locations, and web resources. Career Peers will regularly use this knowledge to effectively answer questions, concerns, or requests that come in at the main office’s front desk, whether through in-person visits, email or incoming phone calls from students, alumni, employers, faculty, and staff. The majority of the student experience role will involve managing the walk-in program, answering phones, and checking students/alumni in for appointments as they arrive. During down-time, in the office, Career Peers will also enter collected survey data and assist with office projects. Career Peers will also serve as outreach specialists to promote Career Services to the campus community through presentations and peer to peer outreach. Career Peers will serve as a Career Services student representative at university-sponsored events. Upon completion of training and demonstrated skill development, Career Peers will deliver presentations to student organizations and residence halls on Career Services programs and resources. Career Peers will also assist in Career Services special events, activities, programs or day to day operations. BENEFITS TO STUDENT As Career Peers, students will: • Gain thorough knowledge of foundational career development tools and software • Develop and enhance leadership, presentation, and coaching skills • Build relations with Career Services and university faculty, staff and students • Network with ECU alumni and employers during Career Services events • Develop professional etiquette and enhance professional presence • Gain administrative and transferable office setting skills As employees in the Division of Student Affairs, students will have the opportunity to gain the following competencies based on a framework of core and recommended career development competencies established by the Division of Student Affairs and the National Association of Colleges and Employers. Effective Communication (Written and Verbal) CORE : Ability to listen effectively and relay information via written, verbal, and non-verbal means in a way that is understood by target audience. Problem Solving/Effective Reasoning CORE : Ability to identify challenges and form alternative solutions and approaches to problems using logic and effective reasoning while maintaining the integrity of all individuals/organizations. Team Work CORE : Ability to cooperate and work effectively with others to achieve a common goal or outcome. Accountability/Integrity CORE : Ability to build on personal and ethical foundation while demonstrating integrity, responsibility, and dependability to do assigned tasks with minimal supervision while maintaining a professional level of trust. Adaptability/Resiliency CORE : Demonstrating flexibility in the face of changing circumstances and responding proactively to adversity. Professionalism: Ability to demonstrate good customer service skills and professionalism in attitude/demeanor and disposition that makes one approachable and relatable to others. Organization/Planning: Ability to show efficiency in completing assigned tasks through planning, prioritizing, time-management, and effective use of available resources. GPA Requirement Minimum of 2.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Candidate must be able to work flexible schedule up to 5-20 hours per week from 8am-5pm. Desired candidate will display an interest in promoting Career Services and assisting peers in achieving desired goals and career outcomes. License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload your Resume, Federal Work Study Hiring Authorization Form, and a copy of your Fall class schedule online. To be ELIGIBLE for FEDERAL WORK STUDY POSITIONS , students MUST QUALIFY and RECEIVE an AWARD from the ECU Financial Aid Office (Old Cafeteria Complex, 252 328-6610.) Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95579 Open Date 07/23/2026 Close Date 04/01/2027 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Federal Work Study Hiring Authorization Additional Document #1 Optional Documents Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95991": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Hourly Student Employment - Student Technicians Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Hourly Student Employment - Student Technicians Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department LIBRARY SERVICES-JOYNER Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Hourly Student Employment - Student Technicians Posting Number 08473 Position Number 08473 Student Job Category Student - Hourly Job Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 2 Rate of Pay $10.00 - $14.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description ECU Department of Library Services- Joyner is currently seeking Student Technicians to provide technical support to students, faculty, and staff at the Technology & Printing Services desk located on the first floor of Joyner Library. Duties: (Primary Duty) Assist ECU students, faculty and staff with technology-related issues. These issues include, but are not limited to printing support, onboarding personal devices to the campus’ Wi-Fi network, and assistance with basic software and hardware questions. Processing and printing poster requests. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Candidates must have good communication skills. This position requires effective and clear communication with department staff as well as ECU students, faculty, and staff who use the library. Familiarity with technology, including Microsoft Word, Outlook, PowerPoint, Adobe Acrobat, and basic printing knowledge. Candidates must be able to maintain an organized shared work environment. Candidates must be in good academic standing with East Carolina University. GPA Requirement Minimum of 2.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload your Resume online. Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95937 Open Date 07/31/2026 Close Date 09/14/2026 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Optional Documents Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96593": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Hourly Student Employment - CLCE Student Leadership Assistants Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Hourly Student Employment - CLCE Student Leadership Assistants Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department STUDENT LIFE Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Hourly Student Employment - CLCE Student Leadership Assistants Posting Number 08412 Position Number 08412 Student Job Category Student - Hourly Job Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 1 Rate of Pay $12.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description ECU Department of Student Life is currently seeking several CLCE Student Leadership Assistants. The SLA will strive to support a welcoming environment which fosters education through leadership and service. The primary role of a Student Leadership Assistant is to support the mission of CLCE . This includes: • Daily office admin operations include greeting visitors, checking mail, answering phones, and organizing files. • Assist office staff with CLCE programs and events. This includes leadership, service, and voter engagement programs and initiatives here at ECU . • Lead and facilitate different initiatives such as: Alternative Break Experiences, Chancellor’s Student Leadership Academy, Citizen U, LeaderShape, Pirates GIVE , and Pirates VOTE . • Serve as a student leader for one Pirates Give Day of Service and plan at least one to two Pirates Give Pop Up Service events per semester. • Manage and recruit participants and volunteers for CLCE programs and events. • Attend outreach events that promote CLCE related programs and events (weekly tabling events, university sponsored visitation days, etc.) • Assist with ECU’s Williams-Ross Purple Pantry duties including managing inventory, coordinating deliveries, donations, and events with community partners. • Attend monthly Student Leadership Assistant leadership meetings to discuss upcoming events and tasks GPA Requirement Minimum of 2.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) Must be in good academic standing Must be enrolled in Fall 2026 and/or Spring 2027 Ability to work a consistent weekly schedule during Fall and/or Spring semester. Strong communication, organization, and customer service skills preferred Ability to lift and move items (light to moderate lifting) and be comfortable working in a fast-paced, service oriented environment $12.00/hour (contingent upon experience). Student Leadership Assistants can work 10 hours per week and 20 hours per pay period. License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload resume online All offers of employment are conditional and subject to verification of background information, with satisfactory results required before the start of the position. Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95630 Open Date 08/20/2026 Close Date 10/01/2026 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Optional Documents List of References Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to