    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96347": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal | Federal Work Study (On-Campus) - Office Assistant",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Federal Work Study (On-Campus) - Office Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Federal Work Study (On-Campus) - Office Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department EMPLOYMENT SERVICES Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Federal Work Study (On-Campus) - Office Assistant Posting Number 08389 Position Number 08389 Student Job Category Student - Federal Work Study On-Campus Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 1 Rate of Pay $10.00 /hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description The Department of Finance is seeking a Federal Work-Study Student Assistant to support Finance faculty members with the review, organization, and preparation of course materials and documents to help ensure courses meet ADA accessibility standards. The student will also assist with departmental communications and other administrative projects as needed. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Assist Finance faculty members with course materials and documents to help make courses ADA compliant. Review, organize, and format instructional materials for accessibility. Assist with updating electronic course content and files. Perform other administrative and clerical duties as assigned in support of the Finance Department. GPA Requirement Minimum of 2.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload your Resume and Federal Work Study Authorization Form online. To be ELIGIBLE for FEDERAL WORK STUDY POSITIONS , students MUST QUALIFY and RECEIVE an AWARD from the ECU Financial Aid Office (Old Cafeteria Complex, 252-328-6610.) Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95552 Open Date 07/23/2025 Close Date 04/01/2027 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you been approved for federal work study? (Please note that you will need to add your federal work study authorization form online). Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Federal Work Study Hiring Authorization Optional Documents Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
