    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96014": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Hourly Student Employment - Well-Being Ambassadors/Well-Being Coaches Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Hourly Student Employment - Well-Being Ambassadors/Well-Being Coaches Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department CAMPUS RECREATION AND WELLNESS Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Hourly Student Employment - Well-Being Ambassadors/Well-Being Coaches Posting Number 08372 Position Number 08372 Student Job Category Student - Hourly Job Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 30 Rate of Pay $11.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description ECU Department of Campus Recreation and Wellness is currently seeking several Well-Being Ambassadors/Well-Being Coaches. Campus Recreation and Wellness ( CRW ) strives to promote, organize, and administer structured, self-directed, educationally oriented and leadership development programs and services to enhance positive recreation and wellness lifestyles of the university community. CRW is committed to imparting a sense of responsible citizenship, providing relevant student leadership experiences, enhancing individual potential, and fostering a lifelong commitment to learning skills associated with physical, social, emotional, and mental well-being. CRW supports the Division of Student Affairs commitment to purposeful well-being. We strive to enhance the vitality and resilience of our students and campus community. Please visit https://crw.ecu.edu/about-us/join-the-crw-team/job-descriptions/ to view the job descriptions and a list of available positions. Well-Being Ambassador duties include: Exhibit an understanding and knowledge of ECU , Well-Being Collective, and Campus Recreation and Wellness ( CRW ) programs, operations, organizational structure, and standard policies and procedures. Provide a world class member experience within a comprehensive well-being program aligning with the five (5) essential elements of well-being: career, social, financial, physical, community. Assist in the content delivery and promotion of various public health programs including alcohol & other drugs, mental health & stress management, sexual health & healthy relationships, nutrition & body image, problem gambling awareness, and overall well-being related topics to constituents both on and off campus. Research, create, and copywrite well-being related content for digital and print media. Create educational content, programs, and support aligning with the program indicators of discover, explore, and live. Contribute innovative ideas and methods to introduce well-being to the campus community. Serve as an active team member on one or more well-being related events and programs (i.e. Fresh Check Day, #YouMatterECU Pop Up, Safe Spring Break, Breakfast On the Go, Pledge Purple, Pleasure Principle, American Heart Walk, etc). Support the Collegiate Recovery Community ( CRC ) by assisting in creating a positive and supportive environment for students in recovery from alcohol, drugs, and other behavioral addictions. Understand and utilize any software applications and programs necessary in accordance with protocols and operations. Solicit and incorporate feedback from a variety of sources (e.g., participants, peers, supervisors, self) to enhance professionalism and future experiences. Enhance competency by using credible resources, attending in-services, and focusing on professional development. Use appropriate verbal and nonverbal communication techniques when interacting with or answering questions from members and guests. Adapt and accommodate a large spectrum of individual personality styles and differences in backgrounds when building rapport and providing assistance to members and guests. Other duties as assigned. Well-Being Coach duties includes: Establish rapport with clients using effective communication strategies to build and maintain collaborative relationships. Help clients take responsibility for personal health by identifying strengths, challenges, and available resources to make healthful lifestyle choices. Facilitate client-directed behavior change using evidence-based coaching strategies to promote healthful lifestyle choices. Use available health, medical, wellness, and lifestyle information by employing appropriate assessment tools and standards to stratify risk, identify the need for medical clearance and referrals, establish baselines and facilitate plan development. Design individualized plans based on interviews, screenings, assessment data, and goals to progress clients toward healthful lifestyle management. Implement individualized plans using evidence-based coaching practices to progress clients toward healthful lifestyle and behavior change. Evaluate plan effectiveness in collaboration with clients to monitor outcomes and support progress toward goals. Collaborate with clients to adjust plans based on ongoing evaluations to promote adherence, personal responsibility, and success. Adhere to legal requirements, the Code of Ethics, and scope-of-practice guidelines to protect clients, maintain professional standards, and manage risk. Maintain accurate and confidential records using applicable standards to ensure quality care and manage risk. Respond to emergencies and high-risk situations following established protocols to ensure safety and reduce liability. Maintain professional competence by staying current on research, technology, and industry standards to build proficiency as a health coach and optimize client outcomes. Create a welcoming environment by developing awareness of, and demonstrating sensitivity to, various populations. Solicit and incorporate feedback from a variety of sources (e.g., participants, peers, supervisors, self) to enhance professionalism and future experiences. Other duties as assigned. GPA Requirement Minimum of 2.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) Well-Being Ambassadors: Valid CPR / AED and First Aid certification and blood-borne pathogens training within 60 days of hire. NASPA Certified Peer Educator training within 60 days of hire. Completion of HLTH 1000 or other health related courses. Demonstrated proficiency in Microsoft Office365. Ability to work independently and as a team for a minimum of 5-12 hours per week. Flexible work availability required included but not limited to the early morning, nights, weekends, holidays, and ECU sanctioned breaks. Well-Being Coaches: Valid CPR / AED and First Aid certification and blood-borne pathogens training within 60 days of hire. NASPA Certified Peer Educator training within 60 days of hire. NCCA (National Commission for Certifying Agencies) accredited health and/or well-being certification or ability to obtain within 60 days of hire. License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload your resume online as it relates to your area of interest. Please list your Expected Date of Graduation Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95509 Open Date 07/23/2026 Close Date 09/06/2026 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have any related certifications? If so, please list those certifications as well as the expiration date. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96604": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Hourly Student Employment - Campus Tour Guides/Pirate Navigators Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Hourly Student Employment - Campus Tour Guides/Pirate Navigators Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department ADMISSIONS Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Hourly Student Employment - Campus Tour Guides/Pirate Navigators Posting Number 08586 Position Number 08586 Student Job Category Student - Hourly Job Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 100 Rate of Pay $11.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description ECU Office of Undergraduate Admissions is currently seeking personable, energetic, and enthusiastic students to serve as Tour Guides/Pirate Navigators. Tour Guides play an important role in welcoming prospective students, families, and other campus visitors to East Carolina University. In this position, students will lead engaging and informative campus tours while sharing valuable information about ECU’s academic programs, campus facilities, student life, history, traditions, and resources. Tour Guides are expected to create a welcoming and interactive experience for guests, answer questions, and represent ECU and the Office of Undergraduate Admissions in a positive and professional manner. Additional responsibilities may include assisting with Admissions events, supporting office initiatives, and completing other duties as assigned. Work Schedule Tour Guide shifts are primarily scheduled Monday through Friday during the following time blocks: 9:00 a.m. – 12:00 p.m. 12:00 p.m. – 3:00 p.m. 2:00 p.m. – 5:00 p.m. Special Admissions Events (Open House, Pirate Nation Bound, etc.) will include Saturdays Schedules may vary based on campus visit and event needs. GPA Requirement Minimum of 2.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. Students are encouraged to apply early, as positions may be filled throughout the recruitment period. Please upload your resume online. Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96573 Open Date 08/21/2026 Close Date 10/04/2026 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Optional Documents Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95309": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal | Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. East Carolina University requires applicants to submit a candidate profile online in order to be considered for the position. In addition to submitting a candidate profile online, please submit online the following required applicant documents: • Curriculum Vitae • Letter of Interest • List of two to three original letters of reference (noting contact information) At the time of employment, two to three original letters of reference, official transcripts, a criminal background check, and proper documentation of identity and employability are required. Please be aware that if selected as the candidate of choice, an automatic e-mail will be sent to the individuals entered by the applicant in the References section of the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system. Letters of reference submitted via the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system will be verified and considered towards meeting this requirement. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor Position Number 976133 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Department AAH CON Nursing Science Department Homepage https://nursing.ecu.edu/ Advertising Department NURSING-COLLEGE OF Division Academic Affairs Classification Title Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor Working Title Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor Number of Vacancies 3 Full Time Equivalent (FTE) 1.0 Full Time or Part Time Full Time Anticipated Recruitment Range. Salary offered may be outside of this range as impacted by budget, UNC salary administration, and/or candidate qualifications. Commensurate with Qualifications Position Location (City) Greenville Position Type Faculty (Teaching) Job Category Faculty (Teaching) Organizational Unit Overview The mission of the college is to serve as a national model for transforming the health of rural underserved regions through excellence and innovation in nursing education, leadership, research, scholarship, and practice. The ECU College of Nursing continuously strives to create a learning environment and workplace culture that provides opportunity, support, and consideration for all students, employees, alumni, and other stakeholders. Job Duties The East Carolina University College of Nursing ( ECUCON ), Department of Nursing Science seeks applicants for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position. Academic appointment will be commensurate with the qualifications of the applicant. Responsibilities for the Nursing Science Department position include: Maintaining an active program of research in an area relevant to the mission of the college Establishing a funded program of research. Producing scholarly works, including peer-reviewed publications and presentations at state, national, and/or international levels. Teaching, developing, and evaluating relevant courses within the undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs. Providing academic advisement and research mentorship to doctoral and Honors College students. Chairing and serving on PhD dissertation committees. Participating in shared governance through college and university-level committee work. Attend one day per week for meetings and committee work. Contingent upon the availability of funds. Minimum Education/Experience An earned PhD in nursing (or related field, plus a master’s degree in nursing ) or an EdD (plus a master’s degree in nursing) at the time of hire. Qualifying degrees must be received from accredited institutions. Evidence of a developed or developing research trajectory. Effective written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. License or Certification Required by Statute or Regulation A valid non-restricted North Carolina registered nurse license is required upon employment. Preferred Experience, Skills, Training/Education In-person and Online teaching experience in a university or college setting is preferred. Special Instructions to Applicant East Carolina University requires applicants to submit a candidate profile online in order to be considered for the position. In addition to submitting a candidate profile online, please submit online the following required applicant documents: • Curriculum Vitae • Letter of Interest • List of two to three original letters of reference (noting contact information) At the time of employment, two to three original letters of reference, official transcripts, a criminal background check, and proper documentation of identity and employability are required. Please be aware that if selected as the candidate of choice, an automatic e-mail will be sent to the individuals entered by the applicant in the References section of the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system. Letters of reference submitted via the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system will be verified and considered towards meeting this requirement. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Additional Instructions to Applicant In order to be considered for this position, applicants must complete a candidate profile online via the PeopleAdmin system and submit any requested documents. Additionally, applicants that possess the preferred education and experience must also possess the minimum education/experience, if applicable. Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Job Open Date 06/03/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Job Close Date - Positions will be posted until 11:59 p.m. EST on this date. If no closing date is indicated, the position may close at any time after the initial screening date. Initial Screening Begins 07/03/2026 Rank Level Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/94157 Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu. Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate where you learned about this job vacancy. LinkedIn Chronicle of Higher Education CareerBuilder Greenville Daily Reflector Raleigh News & Observer HigherEdJobs.com InsideHigherEd.com Monster.com Indeed ECU Website Other * Will you now or in the future require visa sponsorship for employment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation Licenses/Certifications Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95867": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Hourly Student Employment - Learning Assistants Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Hourly Student Employment - Learning Assistants Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department FOREIGN LANG & LIT, DEPT OF Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Hourly Student Employment - Learning Assistants Posting Number 08370 Position Number 08370 Student Job Category Student - Hourly Job Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 9 Rate of Pay $11.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? Yes Job Description ECU Department of Foreign Languages and Literatures is currently seeking several Learning Assistants to fulfill the following duties: Assist instructors in class. Help facilitate and lead cultural immersion activities outside class. Assist instructors and students with assignment preparation. Serve as conversation partners for beginning language learners in and outside class. Tutor students, as needed. GPA Requirement Minimum of 3.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) Students who are pursuing a B. A. in Foreign Languages and Literatures; a B.A. in Multidisciplinary Studies with a concentration in Russian Studies; or a minor in Classical Studies, French, Foreign Language Education, German, Hispanic Studies, or Russian Studies are preferred. License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload the days/times you are AVAILABLE to assist instructors in class during common meeting times for our classes: (Monday, Wednesday, and Friday from 10-10:50 a.m. or 11-11:50 a.m. or 12-12:50 p.m. or 1-1:50 p.m., or Monday and Wednesday from 2-3:15 p.m.), your resume, and a cover letter online. Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. All offers of employment are conditional and subject to verification of background information, with satisfactory results required before the start of the position. Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95507 Open Date 07/29/2026 Close Date 09/15/2026 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your major of study? (Open Ended Question) * What is your Grade Point Average (GPA)? (Open Ended Question) * What is your current year of study? Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate * What are your hours of availability? (Open Ended Question) * Have you worked as a learning assistant in lecture or lab at ECU before? If so, which course(s) did you work with? (Include department and course number) (Open Ended Question) * Has an ECU faculty member requested that you apply as a learning assistant to work in their class, if so, please list the name(s) of the faculty and the course number. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Cover Letter Additional Document #1 Optional Documents Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96898": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal | Dr. Leroy T. Walker Professorship Associate Professor or Professor",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Dr. Leroy T. Walker Professorship Associate Professor or Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Dr. Leroy T. Walker Professorship Associate Professor or Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In order to apply, candidates must submit the following materials online at www.jobs.ecu.edu: 1. Cover letter addressing position description How the applicant’s education, experience, and goals align with job duties. Plan for use of an annual operations budget (if funds are available). 2. Curriculum Vitae/Resume 3. A list of three references with contact information. As part of the screening process, the references provided may be contacted. At the time of employment two to three original letters of reference, official transcripts, a criminal background check, and proper documentation of identity and employability are required. Applicants must complete a candidate profile by creating an account (see “Create Account” by following link below) online via the PeopleAdmin system (https://ecu.peopleadmin.com) Please be aware that if selected as a candidate of choice, an automatic e-mail will be sent to the individuals entered by the applicant in the References section of the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system. Letters of reference submitted via the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system will be verified and considered towards meeting this requirement. For letters of reference not submitted via the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system, please have the original signed letters mailed to Lee Gaylord (Walker Professorship) East Carolina University, College of Health and Human Performance 1000 East 5th Street, Rivers West 238 Mail Stop 505, Greenville, NC 27858. For questions, please reach out to Dr. Alice Richman, RICHMANA@ECU.EDU. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Position Details Position Information Job Title Dr. Leroy T. Walker Professorship Associate Professor or Professor Position Number DPHHS26 Vacancy Open to ECU Employees Department AAH Col of Health and Human Sci Department Homepage https://chhs.ecu.edu/ Advertising Department HLTH/HUMAN PERF,COLLEGE OF Division Academic Affairs Classification Title Dr. Leroy T. Walker Distinguished Professorship, Associate Professor or Professor Working Title Dr. Leroy T. Walker Distinguished Professorship, Associate Professor or Professor Number of Vacancies 1 Full Time Equivalent (FTE) 0.0 Full Time or Part Time Part Time Anticipated Recruitment Range. Salary offered may be outside of this range as impacted by budget, UNC salary administration, and/or candidate qualifications. Commensurate with Qualifications Position Type Faculty (Teaching) Position Location (City) Greenville Job Category Faculty (Teaching) Be a Pirate! Be a Pirate! East Carolina University ( ECU ) is consistently ranked among the nation’s top public universities for its commitment to research, innovation, social mobility, and public service. Classified as a R1 institution by the Carnegie Commission on Higher Education, ECU is among the top 5% of research universities in the United States, an elite designation reflecting the highest levels of research activity, funding, and doctoral output. Founded in 1907, ECU is a public, four-year university located in Greenville, N.C. , which and is widely regarded as the cultural, educational, economic, and medical hub of eastern North Carolina. Through education, research, healthcare, community engagement, athletics, cultural enrichment, and service, ECU enhances the quality of life for its students, the state and communities around the world. It is a great place to work, teach, and learn. ECU’s commitment to impactful scholarship is further demonstrated through its repeated Carnegie Community Engagement Classification (2010, 2015, 2024), as well as its 2024 designation as a Carnegie Leadership for Public Purpose institution. These distinctions recognize the university’s leadership in translating research into meaningful community partnerships and measurable societal benefits. The university supports its workforce through a wide range of professional development opportunities designed to foster career growth and skill advancement. Eligible employees also benefit from a comprehensive benefits package that promotes a healthy work-life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The College of Health and Human Sciences at East Carolina University is committed to improving the quality of life and health of individuals, families, and communities across North Carolina and beyond. Through its certificate, bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral programs, the College prepares students to deliver professional and clinical services, conduct impactful research, and develop innovative, real-world solutions that promote healthier lives and lasting positive change. The College values experiential learning, with faculty and students working side by side in classrooms, clinics, laboratories, and community settings to advance excellence in education, research, and service. Students are empowered to discover their purpose while preparing for meaningful careers that improve lives, strengthen communities, and advance health and wellness in a wide range of professional fields. Primary Purpose of Position INTERNAL POSTING : Open only to applicants currently employed by East Carolina University. Professorship is open only to current full-time members who are tenured and hold the rank of Associate Professor or Professor (excluding those whose primary responsibilities are in administration) in the College of Health and Human Sciences. The faculty member selected for this professorship will: 1. Lead and promote interdisciplinary research, innovative approaches to instruction, and serve as a resource for others regarding issues related to a) building a more peaceful and better world through sport (i.e. sport for development as envisioned by the International Olympic Committee, United States Olympic Committee, United Nations, World Health Organization, Unicef, etc.) and/or b) the development of athletes from a holistic perspective (e.g. performance or wellbeing) in the Olympic spirit exemplified by Dr. Walker. 2. Engage and collaborate with campus leaders and community members; local, national, and international agencies and organizations; and others with interests related to sport for development and/or an aspect of holistic athlete development. 3. Share the work supported by this professorship with academic, professional, and public audiences. Participate in outreach and donor relations relevant to this professorship (e.g. provide a tour of a lab to a member of the family the professorship honors, include reference to the professorship in professional email signatures and other appropriate contexts, and otherwise represent the professorship in a positive manner). The initial appointment of the professorship will be for a 3-year term and may be renewed. Contingent upon availability of funds. Minimum Education, Knowledge, Skills, and Experience Associate Professor or Professor with a tenure home in a unit within the College of Health and Human Sciences at East Carolina University. (Associate Professors are eligible to be appointed as a Leroy T. Walker Distinguished Scholar; Professors are eligible to be appointed as a Leroy T. Walker Distinguished Professor) License or Certification Required by Statute or Regulation None Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills, and Experience None Special Instructions to Applicant In order to apply, candidates must submit the following materials online at www.jobs.ecu.edu: 1. Cover letter addressing position description How the applicant’s education, experience, and goals align with job duties. Plan for use of an annual operations budget (if funds are available). 2. Curriculum Vitae/Resume 3. A list of three references with contact information. As part of the screening process, the references provided may be contacted. At the time of employment two to three original letters of reference, official transcripts, a criminal background check, and proper documentation of identity and employability are required. Applicants must complete a candidate profile by creating an account (see “Create Account” by following link below) online via the PeopleAdmin system (https://ecu.peopleadmin.com) Please be aware that if selected as a candidate of choice, an automatic e-mail will be sent to the individuals entered by the applicant in the References section of the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system. Letters of reference submitted via the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system will be verified and considered towards meeting this requirement. For letters of reference not submitted via the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system, please have the original signed letters mailed to Lee Gaylord (Walker Professorship) East Carolina University, College of Health and Human Performance 1000 East 5th Street, Rivers West 238 Mail Stop 505, Greenville, NC 27858. For questions, please reach out to Dr. Alice Richman, RICHMANA@ECU. EDU . Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Additional Instructions to Applicant Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Job Open Date 09/01/2026 Job Close Date - Positions will be posted until 11:59 p.m. EST on this date. If no closing date is indicated, the position may close at any time after the initial screening date. 09/15/2026 Initial Screening Begins Rank Level Professor, Associate Professor Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96837 Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. If highest degree earned is from an institution outside of the U.S. and its territories, final candidates are required to have their degree validated as equivalent to the degree conferred by a regionally accredited college or university in the U.S. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu. Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you now or in the future require visa sponsorship for employment? Yes No * Are you currently an ECU Employee? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Additional Document #1 Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
