      "title": "East Carolina University Portal | Federal Work Study (Off-Campus) - NC Stop Human Trafficking - Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Federal Work Study (Off-Campus) - NC Stop Human Trafficking - Administrative Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Federal Work Study (Off-Campus) - NC Stop Human Trafficking - Administrative Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department OFF CAMPUS STUDENT EMPLOYER Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Federal Work Study (Off-Campus) - NC Stop Human Trafficking - Administrative Assistant Posting Number 08379 Position Number 08379 Student Job Category Student - Federal Work Study Community Service Position Location Off-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 1 Rate of Pay $12.00 - $14.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description NC Stop Human Trafficking is seeking an administrative assistant to assist with office operations. Tasks include, but are not limited to: Register for events Make travel plans Send correspondence Manage day-to-day operations of office Manage email and contacts Manage paperwork with bookkeeper Record-keeping of speaking engagements, events Post on Social Media Manage inventory Order products Update inventory Price tags/signs GPA Requirement Minimum of 2.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) Excellent written communication skills Ability to organize and manage work time Proficiency in Microsoft Office (including Word, Excel, and PowerPoint) Proficiency in Google Business (Gmail, calendar, Google Drive) Access to reliable transportation License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please submit a hiring authorization form, resume, cover letter, and three references to: Pam Str