    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95949": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Federal Work Study - Box Office/Theatre Assistants Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Federal Work Study - Box Office/Theatre Assistants Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department THEATRE&DANCE,SCH OF Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Federal Work Study - Box Office/Theatre Assistants Posting Number 08434 Position Number 08434 Student Job Category Student - Federal Work Study On-Campus Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 14 Rate of Pay $10.00 - $14.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? Yes Job Description ECU School of Theatre and Dance is seeking several enthusiastic and reliable Box Office/Theatre Assistants to support the Box Office Manager with ticket sales, customer inquiries, and various administrative tasks related to the ECU /Loessin Playhouse operations and marketing including social media, website, and visual promotions. This role involves direct interaction with the public, requiring strong customer service skills and professionalism both in-person and over the phone. Key Responsibilities: Assist with ticket sales and patron communications Respond to phone messages and emails Support general box office operations Assist with marketing and event advertising Perform miscellaneous duties as assigned by the Box Office Manager Potentially assist in Design & Production shops (e.g., costumes, paint, props) based on experience and availability Work Schedule: Primarily Monday–Friday, 10:00 AM – 4:00 PM Flexible hours to accommodate class schedules Evening and weekend shifts required during Playhouse performances (scheduled in advance) Box office closed during university holidays and breaks Dress Code: Business casual attire during performances or show-specific costumes as directed by the Design Team Casual attire acceptable during non-performance work hours Assignments to Design & Production shops will be discussed during the interview for applicants interested. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and levels of experience. GPA Requirement Minimum of 2.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) Strong communication and customer service skills Ability to work independently and as part of a team Professional demeanor and punctuality Interest or experience in theatre production All majors are welcome, no experience required. License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload your Resume and Federal Work Study Hiring Authorization Form online. To be ELIGIBLE for FEDERAL WORK STUDY POSITIONS , students MUST QUALIFY and RECEIVE an AWARD from the ECU Financial Aid Office (Old Cafeteria Complex, 252-328-6610.) Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. All offers of employment are conditional and subject to verification of background information, with satisfactory results required before the start of the position, Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95731 Open Date 07/31/2026 Close Date 04/01/2027 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you been approved for federal work study? (Please note that you will need to add your federal work study authorization form online). Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Federal Work Study Hiring Authorization Optional Documents Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
