    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96368": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Federal Work Study - ROTC Office Assistants Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Federal Work Study - ROTC Office Assistants Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please upload your Resume and Federal Work Study Hiring Authorization Form online.To be ELIGIBLE for FEDERAL WORK STUDY POSITIONS, students MUST QUALIFY and RECEIVE an AWARD from the ECU Financial Aid Office (Old Cafeteria Complex, 252-328-6610.) Position Details Position Information Advertising Department MILITARY SCIENCE, DEPT OF Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Federal Work Study - ROTC Office Assistants Posting Number 08405 Position Number 08405 Student Job Category Student - Federal Work Study On-Campus Position Location On-campus City Greenville State North Carolina Number of Vacancies 10 Rate of Pay $12.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description ECU Department of Military Science is currently seeking several Office Assistants. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Administrative Support Provide front desk coverage, greet visitors, and assist cadets, staff, and prospective students Answer phones, respond to emails, and route inquiries appropriately Maintain accurate records, files, and databases (digital and physical) Assist with scheduling appointments, meetings, and ROTC events Support preparation of reports, correspondence, and program materials Uniform Issue & Supply Support Assist in issuing, fitting, and collecting ROTC uniforms and equipment Maintain organized inventory of uniforms, supplies, and accessories Track accountability of issued items using established systems Inspect returned uniforms for cleanliness and serviceability Assist with inventory counts and restocking of supplies Ensure proper storage and organization of uniform rooms Cadet & Program Support Assist cadets with uniform questions, fitting, and wear guidance (as trained) Support ROTC training events, orientations, and special functions Help set up and break down for events, briefings, and inspections Maintain confidentiality of cadet and program information Note: This position supports both Army and Air Force ROTC programs and may require coordination between both departments. GPA Requirement Minimum of 2.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) Preferred Qualifications Interest in military service or ROTC programs Experience with inventory management or administrative work Familiarity with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Outlook) Ability to lift and move boxes (up to 25–40 lbs) Ability to stand for extended periods during uniform issue or events Must be eligible for Federal Work-Study Strong organizational and time management skills Professional communication and customer service skills Ability to follow instructions and work independently Attention to detail and accountability Work Schedule Flexible schedule based on academic commitments and office needs May require occasional early morning or late afternoon support for ROTC activities Professional Expectations Maintain a professional appearance and demeanor Demonstrate reliability, punctuality, and integrity Follow ROTC policies and procedures at all times License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload your resume and Federal Work Study Authorization Form online. To be ELIGIBLE for FEDERAL WORK STUDY POSITIONS , students MUST QUALIFY and RECEIVE an AWARD from the ECU Financial Aid Office (Old Cafeteria Complex, 252-328-6610.) Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95639 Open Date 07/28/2026 Close Date 04/01/2027 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Office of Student Financial Aid? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Federal Work Study Hiring Authorization Optional Documents Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96788": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | BSOM Clinical Faculty Advisor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU BSOM Clinical Faculty Advisor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. At the time of employment, two to four original letters of reference, official transcripts, a criminal background check, and proper documentation of identity and employability are required. Please be aware that if selected as Candidate of Choice, an automatic e-mail will be sent to the individuals entered by the applicant in the references section of the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system. Letters of reference submitted via the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system will be verified and considered for meeting this requirement. Position Details Position Information Job Title BSOM Clinical Faculty Advisor Position Number BSOM_Clin_Fac_Advisor Vacancy Open to All Candidates Department EHH BSOM Acad Aff Student Affairs Department Homepage https://medicine.ecu.edu/studentaffairs/ Advertising Department ACADEMIC AFFAIRS-BSOM Division ECU Health/BSOM Classification Title Clinical Assistant Professor, Assistant Professor, Clinical Associate Professor, Associate Professor, Clinical Professor, Professor Working Title BSOM Faculty Advisor Number of Vacancies 16 Full Time Equivalent (FTE) .10 fTE Full Time or Part Time Part Time Anticipated Recruitment Range. Salary offered may be outside of this range as impacted by budget, UNC salary administration, and/or candidate qualifications. Commensurate with Qualifications Position Type Faculty (Teaching) Position Location (City) Greenville Job Category Faculty (Teaching) Be a Pirate! Be a Pirate! East Carolina University ( ECU ) is consistently ranked among the nation’s top public universities for its commitment to research, innovation, social mobility, and public service. Classified as a R1 institution by the Carnegie Commission on Higher Education, ECU is among the top 5% of research universities in the United States, an elite designation reflecting the highest levels of research activity, funding, and doctoral output. Founded in 1907, ECU is a public, four-year university located in Greenville, N.C. , which and is widely regarded as the cultural, educational, economic, and medical hub of eastern North Carolina. Through education, research, healthcare, community engagement, athletics, cultural enrichment, and service, ECU enhances the quality of life for its students, the state and communities around the world. It is a great place to work, teach, and learn. ECU’s commitment to impactful scholarship is further demonstrated through its repeated Carnegie Community Engagement Classification (2010, 2015, 2024), as well as its 2024 designation as a Carnegie Leadership for Public Purpose institution. These distinctions recognize the university’s leadership in translating research into meaningful community partnerships and measurable societal benefits. The university supports its workforce through a wide range of professional development opportunities designed to foster career growth and skill advancement. Eligible employees also benefit from a comprehensive benefits package that promotes a healthy work-life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The mission of the Office of Student Affairs is to create a supportive environment in which medical students may develop personally and professionally, and to maintain records of students’ accomplishments toward their medical school requirements. Primary Purpose of Position This is an “Internal Posting” open only to applicants who are currently permanent BSOM faculty of East Carolina University, Brody School of Medicine or ECU Health-employed Physicians who are currently involved in clinical teaching of Brody School of Medicine medical students. These positions will be part-time (.10 FTE /10%) reassignments of time for Brody School of Medicine faculty members or ECU Health-employed Physicians. Brody School of Medicine Clinical Faculty Advisors play a vital role in fostering belonging, professionalism, wellness, and service aligned with BSOM’s commitment to improving the health of eastern North Carolina. Clinical Faculty Advisors partner with student leaders and collaborate with House Deans to cultivate supportive learning environments across all four years. Clinical Faculty Advisors will report directly to the Brody School of Medicine House Deans. Job Duties: Student Support Responsibilities - 80% Mentor students in professional identity formation and career exploration. Support Learning Community student leaders and community-building efforts. Promote wellbeing and professionalism. Participate in Learning Community programming and reflection activities. Participate in clinical simulation and/or clinical skills sessions to provide direct and formative feedback to assigned students (approximately 4 half-day sessions per academic year) Serve as a primary advisor and mentor for an assigned cohort of medical students, providing guidance on academic concerns, professional, and personal development throughout their medical school journey. Offer career advising and support for residency applications as needed in collaboration with House Deans, including reviewing components of subspecialty specific application system for students in the individual House Dean’s assigned cohort. Serve as a bridge between students and university resources, including BSOM Office of Student Success and Wellness, Student Health, Counseling Services. Other duties as assigned. Learning Community Administrative Responsibilities – 20% Biannual required meetings with assigned students. Monitoring assigned students’ academic performance. Quarterly meetings with House Deans to share community trends and concerns. Other duties as assigned. Time Commitment – Approximately .10 FTE , 16 hours per month Minimum Education, Knowledge, Skills, and Experience MD, DO, or MBBS from an appropriately accredited institution or completed foreign medical education accepted and recognized for ECFMG Certification. Current Brody School of Medicine faculty member at a rank of Clinical Assistant Professor/Assistant Professor or higher or ECU Health-employed Physician who is currently involved in clinical teaching of Brody School of Medicine medical students. Minimum of 1-year post-residency/fellowship training experience as a clinician in a medical educational environment. Demonstrated commitment to student development, mentoring, and support. License or Certification Required by Statute or Regulation Full, unencumbered license to practice medicine in North Carolina. Full schedule DEA Registration Certificate. Credentialing with ECU Physicians and/or privileges with ECU Health. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills, and Experience Prior experience with the education of medical students. Prior leadership experience in pre-clerkship or clerkship medical education, student affairs, or a related area. Commitment to student mentorship and development. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Special Instructions to Applicant Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. At the time of employment, two to four original letters of reference, official transcripts, a criminal background check, and proper documentation of identity and employability are required. Please be aware that if selected as Candidate of Choice, an automatic e-mail will be sent to the individuals entered by the applicant in the references section of the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system. Letters of reference submitted via the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system will be verified and considered for meeting this requirement. Additional Instructions to Applicant In order to be considered for this position, applicants must complete a candidate profile online via the PeopleAdmin system and submit any requested documents. Additionally, applicants that possess the preferred education and experience must also possess the minimum education/experience, if applicable. Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Job Open Date 08/28/2026 Job Close Date - Positions will be posted until 11:59 p.m. EST on this date. If no closing date is indicated, the position may close at any time after the initial screening date. Initial Screening Begins 09/14/2026 Rank Level Not Applicable Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96666 Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. If highest degree earned is from an institution outside of the U.S. and its territories, final candidates are required to have their degree validated as equivalent to the degree conferred by a regionally accredited college or university in the U.S. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu. Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree earned? (Open Ended Question) * Will you now or in the future require visa sponsorship for employment? Yes No * Please indicate where you learned about this job vacancy. LinkedIn Chronicle of Higher Education CareerBuilder Greenville Daily Reflector Raleigh News & Observer HigherEdJobs.com InsideHigherEd.com Monster.com Indeed ECU Website Other * Are you currently a Brody School of Medicine faculty member at a rank of Clinical Assistant Professor/Assistant Professor or higher or an ECU Health-employed Physician who is currently involved in clinical teaching of Brody School of Medicine medical students? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Licenses/Certifications Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
