      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Hourly Student Employment - Multimedia Content Creator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Hourly Student Employment - Multimedia Content Creator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department ACADEMIC & FACULTY DEVELOPMENT Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Hourly Student Employment - Multimedia Content Creator Posting Number 08509 Position Number 08509 Student Job Category Student - Hourly Job Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 1 Rate of Pay $12.50/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description ECU’s Office for Faculty Excellence is currently seeking a Student Multimedia Content Creator to assist with designing and developing instructional resources. Videography experience and interest will be needed, and applicants should be familiar with operating basic video production equipment and basic knowledge of video creation. Must be able to work on campus during the summer. GPA Requirement Minimum of 2.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) Knowledge of video edition applications such as Adobe Premiere or Premiere Rush is preferred but not required. Experience with software (e.g. Adobe Express, Adobe Illustrator, or Adobe Photoshop) for developing visual resources such as flyers and infographics is preferred but not required. License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload your Resume online. Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside