    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95808": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal | Federal Work Study - Communications and Marketing Assistant",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Federal Work Study - Communications and Marketing Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Federal Work Study - Communications and Marketing Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department ANTHROPOLOGY, DEPT OF Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Federal Work Study - Communications and Marketing Assistant Posting Number 08409 Position Number 08409 Student Job Category Student - Federal Work Study On-Campus Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 1 Rate of Pay $14.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description ECU Department of Anthropology is currently seeking a Federal Work Study student to serve as a Communications and Marketing Assistant for the Fall and Spring semesters. This student will assist with promoting departmental events, programs, and initiatives through a variety of print and digital communications while providing general administrative support as needed. Duties Include: Assisting with the creation and scheduling of social media content. Designing department newsletters, flyers, and promotional materials. Coordinating projects with ECU Creative Services and Logo Review to ensure brand compliance. Updating department communications and marketing materials. Photographing and promoting department events and activities, as needed. Assisting faculty and staff with communication and marketing projects as assigned. Performing general office duties as assigned. This position is for the full academic year 2026-27. GPA Requirement Minimum of 3.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) A graduate student is preferred; however, all students will be considered. The department also prefers that the applicant has excellent customer service skills, be detailed oriented, and have the willingness to work with various groups of people. License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload your course schedule, list of references, resume, and Federal Work Study Hiring Authorization Form online. To be ELIGIBLE for FEDERAL WORK STUDY POSITIONS , students MUST QUALIFY and RECEIVE an AWARD from the ECU Financial Aid Office (Old Cafeteria Complex, 252-328-6610.) Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95667 Open Date 07/28/2026 Close Date 04/01/2027 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your ECU Student email address? (Open Ended Question) * What is your major of study? (Open Ended Question) * What is your Grade Point Average (GPA)? (Open Ended Question) * What is your anticipated Graduation Date? (Open Ended Question) * Have you been approved for federal work study? (Please note that you will need to add your federal work study authorization form online). Yes No * What are your hours of availability? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume List of References Federal Work Study Hiring Authorization Additional Document #1 Optional Documents Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/96319": {
      "title": "East Carolina University Portal",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Graduate Hourly Student Employment - Student-Athlete Academic Success Assistants Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Graduate Hourly Student Employment - Student-Athlete Academic Success Assistants Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Advertising Department STUDENT DEVELOPMENT Academic Term/Year FALL 2026/SPRING 2027 Position Title Graduate Hourly Student Employment - Student-Athlete Academic Success Assistants Posting Number 08467 Position Number 08467 Student Job Category Student - Hourly Job Position Location On-campus City Greenville State NC Number of Vacancies 3 Rate of Pay $17.00/hourly FLSA Status FLSA Non-exempt Will the position be subject to the CBC policy? No Job Description ECU Department of Student Development is currently seeking several Student-Athlete Academic Success Assistants, housed in the Athletic Complex, offering graduate employment opportunities designed to prepare emerging professionals for careers in student-athlete academic services and related areas of higher education. The Student-Athlete Academic Success Assistant serves as a graduate-level member of the SAAS team, gaining practical experience in learning support, academic advising, tutor coordination, assessment, and student development within a Division I athletics environment. Responsibilities of this position include: Maintain a caseload of assigned student-athletes receiving academic support services. Assist assigned academic advisors in monitoring student progress, outreach regarding academic concerns and pre-registration meetings. Assist with tutorial program operations, including scheduling, training, and staff support for undergraduate staff. Compile and organize academic data, review program outcomes, and assist with assessment initiatives. Support daily operations of the Student-Athlete Academic Services center. Maintain confidentiality and provide professional level support to student-athletes in accordance ECU , AAC , and NCAA regulations. GPA Requirement Minimum of 3.0 Preferred (Majors, Experience, GPA, etc.) Experience working with students in an academic support, mentoring, advising, tutoring, or educational setting. Experience working in a collegiate athletic services office and/or familiarity with NCAA rules and regulations. Desire to enter the field of Student-Athlete Academic Services. License/certification required Special Instructions to Applicant Please upload your resume and letter of interest online. Additional Instructions to Applicants Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Quick Link for Direct Access https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/95931 Open Date 07/31/2026 Close Date 09/14/2026 Open Until Filled No Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Individuals submitting profiles for these positions must be current ECU students, in good-standing and meet the respective GPA requirement as required by the position type.  Final candidates may be subject to criminal & sex offender background checks based upon the duties and responsibilities of the position. Some vacancies also require motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu . Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * I agree to allow the Office of Student-Athlete Academic Services, Department of Athletics at East Carolina University, to conduct a review of my grades and references to determine my eligibility for employment. I agree I disagree * I understand that my student record pertaining to violations related to the ECU Student Code of Conduct and Academic Integrity, housed in the Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities, will be checked to determine if I meet the minimum expectations for employment by the Office of Student-Athlete Academic Services. I understand. * Please select any of the groups with which you are affiliated Current ECU Student-Athlete Former ECU Student-Athlete Athletic training staff/student staff ECU athletics team manager Member of ECU varsity cheer Member of ECU varsity Dance member of ECU Marching Pirates/Pep Band ECU Athletic Department Intern/GA ECU athletics rostered practice player None of these apply to me. Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Additional Document #1 Optional Documents Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
